        "subject": "Milestone 6 — OpenProject Read Integration",
        "description": {
          "format": "markdown",
          "raw": "**Next.** Read open work items from the tracker, so a startup pack can show what is actually in progress.\n\n**Build:** a connection definition whose token stays in the secret store; a provider adapter for health, project resolution, search and get; a read cache beside the index; and bounded signals in the startup pack.\n\n**Not in scope:** writes, webhooks, or mirroring tickets into Markdown.\n\n**Done when** work items reach startup and focused packs, and with the tracker switched off nothing else behaves differently.",
          "html": "<p class=\"op-uc-p\"><strong>Next.</strong> Read open work items from the tracker, so a startup pack can show what is actually in progress.</p>\n<p class=\"op-uc-p\"><strong>Build:</strong> a connection definition whose token stays in the secret store; a provider adapter for health, project resolution, search and get; a read cache beside the index; and bounded signals in the startup pack.</p>\n<p class=\"op-uc-p\"><strong>Not in scope:</strong> writes, webhooks, or mirroring tickets into Markdown.</p>\n<p class=\"op-uc-p\"><strong>Done when</strong> work items reach startup and focused packs, and with the tracker switched off nothing else behaves differently.</p>"
        },
