        "subject": "Milestone 9 — OpenProject Writes",
        "description": {
          "format": "markdown",
          "raw": "The *stop* half of the loop: a session that changed something says so in the tracker.\n\n**Implement:** comments, status changes and new work items, each proposed first and applied only when asked; every write reads back and compares, because a partial update can still answer success.\n\n**Done when** a wrap can record its work items without anyone opening the tracker.",
          "html": "<p class=\"op-uc-p\">The <em>stop</em> half of the loop: a session that changed something says so in the tracker.</p>\n<p class=\"op-uc-p\"><strong>Implement:</strong> comments, status changes and new work items, each proposed first and applied only when asked; every write reads back and compares, because a partial update can still answer success.</p>\n<p class=\"op-uc-p\"><strong>Done when</strong> a wrap can record its work items without anyone opening the tracker.</p>"
        },
